|{{Plainlist|
*{{Zone|Private Island}} or {{Zone|Gold Mine}} or {{Zone|Deep Caverns}}, without the {{Enchant|Smelting Touch}} enchantment;
* Anywhere else, using the {{Enchant|Silk Touch}} enchantment;}}
|-
|style="vertical-align:top"|[[File:Iron Ingot.png|21px|link=Iron Ingot]][[File:Gold Ingot.png|21px|link=Gold Ingot]] '''Ingots''':
|{{Plainlist|
* {{Zone|Private Island}} or {{Zone|Gold Mine}} or {{Zone|Deep Caverns}}, using the {{Enchant|Smelting Touch}} enchantment;
* Anywhere else, without using the {{Enchant|Silk Touch}} enchantment;
* Similarly, {{Item|Iron Minion|text=Iron}} and {{Item|Gold Minion}}s equipped with an {{Item|Auto Smelter}} will respectively produce {{Item|Iron Ingot|text=Iron}} or {{Item|Gold Ingot}}s instead of the '''Ore Blocks'''.}}
|}
* [[File:Sponge.png|21px|link=]] [[Sulphur|Sulphur Ores]] only spawn during [[Blazing Volcano#Volcanic Eruptions|Volcanic Eruptions]], shot out of the tip of the {{Zone|Blazing Volcano}}, turning into solid blocks upon impact.
* The {{Item|Goblin Pet}} grants {{stat|mns|1250}} on '''Regular Ores''' while [[Block Strength#Mining Penalties|not on the ground]]. This is a hidden buff.
* The {{AN|Strong Arm}} perk from {{HotM|8|small=y}} grants {{stat|mns|5-500}} on '''Pure Ores'''. This is a hidden buff.

== List of Ores ==
{{For|details regarding required {{stat|bp}}|Breaking Power}}

While unofficial, the community has made a distinction on '''Ores'''. 
*If it bears the "ore block" form when found, then it is designated as a [[File:Coal Ore.png|21px|link=]][[File:Iron Ore.png|21px|link=]][[File:Gold Ore.png|21px|link=]][[File:Lapis  Lazuli Ore.png|21px|link=]][[File:Redstone Ore.png|21px|link=]][[File:Emerald Ore.png|21px|link=]][[File:Diamond Ore.png|21px|link=]][[File:Nether Quartz Ore.png|21px|link=]] {{Blue|'''Regular Ore'''}};
* If it bears the texture of the block that is crafted from it, then it is called a [[File:Block of Coal.png|21px|link=]][[File:Block of Iron.png|21px|link=]][[File:Block of Gold.png|21px|link=]][[File:Block of Lapis Lazuli.png|21px|link=]][[File:Block of Redstone.png|21px|link=]][[File:Block of Emerald.png|21px|link=]][[File:Block of Diamond.png|21px|link=]][[File:Block of Quartz.png|21px|link=]] {{Blue|'''Pure Ore'''}}. These drop considerably more loot than their {{Blue|Regular}} counterparts, though they will also take longer to mine because of their higher [[File:Diamond Pickaxe.png|21px|link=]] [[Block Strength]].

